## Audit Trail CSV (Separate File)

For full audit trail, a second CSV file is generated: `<calculation_id>_audit_trail.csv`

| Column Name | Data Type | Description |
|-------------|-----------|-------------|
| calculation_id | string | Links to main results |
| audit_entry_type | string | "data_imputation", "correlation_applied", "validation_warning", etc. |
| esrs_topic | string | Which topic this entry relates to |
| entry_timestamp | datetime | When this audit entry was created |
| entry_description | string | Human-readable description |
| entry_details_json | string | JSON with technical details |

## Validation Rules

1. **Each calculation_id** must have at least one result row
2. **For each ESRS topic assessed**, there should be 1-4 cost category rows (depending on applicability)
3. **Confidence intervals** must satisfy: ci_lower_eur ≤ calculated_cost_eur ≤ ci_upper_eur
4. **Top influence factor contributions** should sum to ≤100% (other factors may contribute remaining percentage)
5. **Suspicious value flags** must have a reason if TRUE
6. **All monetary values** must be in EUR (no currency conversion)
